Types of Small Business Loans in Decatur AL
Understanding different business loan options can help entrepreneurs choose financing that matches their specific needs.

1. Business Term Loans
Business term loans provide a lump sum of financing that borrowers repay over an agreed period, typically with scheduled payments.
These loans may be suitable for business expansion, major purchases, or long-term investments.

2. Business Lines of Credit
A business line of credit allows qualified borrowers to access funds up to an approved credit limit.
This financing option can be useful for managing cash flow, covering unexpected expenses, or purchasing inventory.
Interest is generally charged on the amount borrowed, subject to the agreement's terms.

3. SBA Loans
Small Business Administration (SBA) loan programs support eligible small businesses through participating lenders.
Depending on the program, financing may be used for working capital, equipment, commercial property, or other qualifying business purposes.
Loan approval, guarantees, and eligibility requirements vary.

